 \subsection{How it was found, and what the scores had already said}
 \label{sec:found}
 
 On 2026-08-18, while looking into why the keyword side rarely seemed to matter, I logged the keyword retriever's row counts for ten real queries. All five conversational queries matched zero chunks, and so did a two-word place-name query. Only queries of two or three technical tokens matched anything. The builder had been the same line of code since the system was built, and all four sibling engines carried it. That it had behaved this way on prose queries throughout is an inference from the unchanged code and the replay, since the system keeps no query log.
 
